        {
          "id": "block_dfb3e321",
          "name": "Block 1",
          "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Scoreboard Bug</title>\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Saira+Condensed:wght@700;800&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <style>\n        /*\n         * LUMA-KEY RULES\n         * - The body is the ONLY pure black. It gets keyed out.\n         * - Every color inside the bug stays at or above ~20% luminance,\n         *   so nothing punches holes through the graphic.\n         * - No rgba(0,0,0,x) shadows: they blend toward black and get keyed,\n         *   which causes ragged fringing. Depth comes from colored shadows\n         *   and white sheens instead.\n         *\n         * STREAM-ENCODING RULES (for anyone restyling this block)\n         * This graphic is keyed over live video and sent through an RTMP\n         * encoder at a modest bitrate over bonded cellular. Tested on a\n         * real stream, subtle styling turns into visible artifacts. Keep\n         * every element inside these limits:\n         * - Flat fills. One solid color per cell, banner and frame. No\n         *   gradients: they band and step under compression.\n         * - No translucency. No rgba overlays, sheens, scanlines, grids or\n         *   glass effects: the encoder cannot hold a subtle alpha blend\n         *   frame to frame and it shimmers.\n         * - No glow. No text-shadow or box-shadow blur: it becomes a halo\n         *   of macroblocks. A hard 2px+ offset shadow in a solid color is\n         *   fine if contrast needs it.\n         * - Nothing thinner than 2px. 1px borders, hairline dividers and\n         *   thin accent bars flicker or vanish. Prefer 3px+.\n         * - Mid-saturation colors. Pure red, magenta and neon bleed at the\n         *   edges because the encoder stores color at half resolution\n         *   (4:2:0). Keep saturation below ~85% and avoid red on dark.\n         * - Text at least 24px, bold, with real contrast against its own\n         *   cell. No letter-spacing tricks, no outlines.\n         * - Keep the body pure black and everything else above ~20% luma\n         *   (LUMA-KEY RULES above still apply).\n         *\n         * STRUCTURE RULES (what a restyle must not change)\n         * - Every data-role / data-side attribute, and the element each one\n         *   sits on. overlay-bind.js finds nodes by data-role and writes\n         *   textContent into them; the team name and score live on inner\n         *   spans so re-renders never touch their sibling banners.\n         * - The banner mechanics: .scorebug-container owning a stacking\n         *   context (position:relative; isolation:isolate), .banner at\n         *   z-index:-1 rooted inside the score cell, width:max-content, and\n         *   the clip-path reveal. Restyle their colors, font and radius;\n         *   do not reposition them or reintroduce fixed widths.\n         * - .banner[data-live-hidden] is the hidden state; the binder\n         *   toggles only that attribute and the text.\n         * - No JavaScript in this block. No external assets except the one\n         *   font link (and keep a system fallback in the font stack: the\n         *   kiosk can be offline at load).\n         * - Fixed pixel sizes, designed at 1920x1080. No vw/vh, no\n         *   animations beyond the banner reveal, no transforms on the\n         *   frame.\n         */\n        :root {\n            /* Frame */\n            --frame-top:    #ffffff;\n            --frame-mid:    #e3e8ff;\n            --frame-bottom: #b7c3ff;\n\n            /* Hammers (top row): hot coral -> tangerine */\n            --home-a:    #ff3d6e;\n            --home-b:    #ff8a3d;\n            --home-deep: #c2184f;   /* ~25% luma: safe for shadows */\n\n            /* Pixel Pirates (bottom row): electric cyan -> cobalt */\n            --away-a:    #00d9ff;\n            --away-b:    #3d6bff;\n            --away-deep: #1f4fd6;   /* ~30% luma */\n\n            /* Clock: white tab, violet accent, dark gray digits */\n            --clock-accent: #7c3aed;\n            --clock-text:   #3a3a3a; /* ~23% luma: darkest color in the bug */\n\n            /* Score panels */\n            --panel-top:    #ffffff;\n            --panel-bottom: #dde3ff;\n\n            --font: 'Saira Condensed', 'Arial Narrow', 'Roboto Condensed', Arial, sans-serif;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            background-color: #000000;   /* keyed out */\n            font-family: var(--font);\n            margin: 50px;\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: flex-start;\n            align-items: flex-start;\n            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n        }\n\n        .scorebug-container {\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            width: fit-content;\n            /* Own stacking context: the banners use z-index:-1 to paint\n               BEHIND .scoreboard's frame (so they genuinely emerge from\n               under it) while still painting above everything outside\n               this container. Without this, a negative z-index falls\n               behind the page itself and the banner disappears. */\n            position: relative;\n            isolation: isolate;\n        }\n\n        /* ---------- Main frame ---------- */\n        .scoreboard {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 240px 80px;\n            grid-auto-rows: 44px;\n            gap: 3px;\n            padding: 3px;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg,\n                var(--frame-top) 0%,\n                var(--frame-mid) 55%,\n                var(--frame-bottom) 100%);\n            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);\n        }\n\n        .row {\n            display: contents;\n        }\n\n        /* ---------- Shared cell ---------- */\n        .cell {\n            position: relative;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n            font-weight: 800;\n            line-height: 1;\n        }\n\n        /* Glass sheen across the top half of every cell */\n        .cell::after {\n            content: '';\n            position: absolute;\n            left: 0;\n            right: 0;\n            top: 0;\n            height: 48%;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg,\n                rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.38) 0%,\n                rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08) 100%);\n            pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        /* ---------- Team name cells ---------- */\n        .team {\n            justify-content: flex-start;\n            padding-left: 22px;\n            color: #ffffff;\n        }\n\n        /* Actual name text - data-role=\"teamName\" lives here now, not on\n         * .cell.team itself, so overlay-bind.js's textContent-replacing\n         * re-render never touches the banner elements that are this\n         * node's siblings (see the DOM structure above). Font sizing\n         * moved here from .team since this is now the node shrinkToFit\n         * actually measures/resizes. */\n        .team-name {\n            display: block;\n            width: 218px;   /* 240px cell - 22px left padding, same as before */\n            overflow: hidden;\n            font-size: 27px;\n            letter-spacing: 0.6px;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            white-space: nowrap;\n        }\n\n        /* White accent chip on the leading edge */\n        .team::before {\n            content: '';\n            position: absolute;\n            left: 0;\n            top: 0;\n            bottom: 0;\n            width: 7px;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65) 100%);\n        }\n\n        .hammers-team {\n            background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--home-a) 0%, var(--home-b) 100%);\n            text-shadow: 0 2px 0 var(--home-deep);\n            border-top-left-radius: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .pirates-team {\n            background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--away-a) 0%, var(--away-b) 100%);\n            text-shadow: 0 2px 0 var(--away-deep);\n            border-bottom-left-radius: 5px;\n        }\n\n        /* ---------- Score cells ---------- */\n        .score {\n            justify-content: center;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel-top) 0%, var(--panel-bottom) 100%);\n            /* Banners anchor here now (rightmost element of each team's\n               row) - .cell's overflow:hidden would otherwise clip them,\n               same reasoning .team used to need before the banners moved\n               here - see the .score-value split below for why data-role\n               lives on an inner span rather than this cell directly. */\n            overflow: visible;\n        }\n\n        .score-value {\n            font-size: 36px;\n            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;   /* no width jump 9 -> 10 */\n        }\n\n        /* Team-colored base bar under each score */\n        .score::before {\n            content: '';\n            position: absolute;\n            left: 0;\n            right: 0;\n            bottom: 0;\n            height: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .hammers-score {\n            color: var(--home-a);\n            text-shadow: 0 2px 0 rgba(194, 24, 79, 0.28);\n            border-top-right-radius: 5px;\n        }\n        .hammers-score::before {\n            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--home-a), var(--home-b));\n        }\n\n        .pirates-score {\n            color: var(--away-b);\n            text-shadow: 0 2px 0 rgba(31, 79, 214, 0.25);\n            border-bottom-right-radius: 5px;\n        }\n        .pirates-score::before {\n            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--away-a), var(--away-b));\n        }\n\n        /* ---------- Clock tab ---------- */\n        .timer-box {\n            position: relative;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            width: 112px;\n            height: 38px;\n            margin-left: 10px;\n            border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel-top) 0%, var(--panel-bottom) 100%);\n            box-shadow:\n                inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9),\n                inset 0 -4px 0 var(--clock-accent);   /* violet base bar */\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n        }\n\n        .timer-box::after {\n            content: '';\n            position: absolute;\n            left: 2px;\n            right: 2px;\n            top: 0;\n            height: 45%;\n            background: linear-gradient(180deg,\n                rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35) 0%,\n                rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 100%);\n            pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        .timer-text {\n            position: relative;\n            z-index: 1;\n            font-size: 28px;\n            font-weight: 800;\n            letter-spacing: 1px;\n            line-height: 1;\n            margin-bottom: 2px;                   /* optically center above the base bar */\n            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;   /* clock digits don't wobble */\n            color: var(--clock-text);\n            text-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);   /* light emboss, no dark fringe */\n        }\n\n        /* .cell has overflow:hidden (keeps the glass-sheen pseudo-element\n         * and the accent chip from poking out) - but a banner needs to\n         * extend PAST its own team cell's right edge to emerge from\n         * behind it, so .team specifically needs that un-clipped. Doesn't\n         * affect .team::before (the accent chip) or .cell::after (the\n         * sheen), since both of those stay fully inside the cell's own\n         * bounds regardless of overflow. */\n        /* ---------- Timeout / penalty banners ----------\n         * Anchored to the RIGHT EDGE of each team's SCORE cell (the\n         * rightmost element of that team's row - .score is\n         * position:relative, so left:100% lands exactly at its right\n         * border) and grows its WIDTH out from 0 - not a position slide -\n         * so it visually emerges from behind that team's nameplate, per\n         * the real desired effect (not a box that slides in from\n         * off-screen). overflow:hidden + white-space:nowrap keeps the\n         * text clipped to whatever width has grown so far, rather than\n         * wrapping or overflowing mid-animation.\n         * Same LUMA-safe rule as everything else in this file: no pure\n         * black, no rgba(0,0,0,x) shadows - colored shadows/borders only.\n         * data-role/data-side live directly on THIS element (not a child\n         * span) because overlay-bind.js reads data-side off the same node\n         * it matched by data-role, and toggles data-live-hidden on that\n         * same node too - see public/overlay-bind.js's renderNode.\n         */\n        .banner {\n            position: absolute;\n            left: calc(100% - 20px);   /* roots 20px inside the score cell, hidden behind the frame */\n            top: 3px;                  /* inset from the row's corners so nothing peeks past the frame's 8px rounding */\n            bottom: 3px;\n            /* Sized to its own text, never a fixed width. The slide is a\n               clip-path reveal from the frame side: hidden clips the whole\n               box (a max-width of 0 can't go below the padding and left a\n               stub showing), shown clips nothing. */\n            width: max-content;\n            clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0);\n            overflow: hidden;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: flex-start;\n            white-space: nowrap;\n            /* Left padding = the 20px hidden root + the frame's 3px edge\n               + a 16px visible gap before the first letter. */\n            padding: 0 18px 0 39px;\n            font-size: 27px;\n            font-weight: 800;\n            letter-spacing: 0.6px;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            color: #ffffff;\n            /* Behind the frame: .scorebug-container isolates a stacking\n               context (see above), so -1 paints under .scoreboard's\n               opaque gradient and the banner's root is truly hidden -\n               no cover strip needed, and nothing sticks out past the\n               frame's edge. */\n            z-index: -1;\n            border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;\n            transition: clip-path 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);\n        }\n\n        .banner[data-live-hidden] {\n            clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0);\n        }\n\n        /* Grown width when active - wide enough for \"Timeout 2:00\" or a\n         * player name at this font size; text itself still clips via the\n         * element's own overflow:hidden if a name runs unusually long. */\n        .banner:not([data-live-hidden]) {\n            clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0);\n        }\n\n        /* Timeout: violet, matches --clock-accent so it reads as \"clock\n         * event\" the same way the timer tab does. Penalty: a warm red\n         * that still clears ~20% luma (LUMA-KEY RULES above). */\n        .timeout-banner {\n            background: linear-gradient(100deg, #9163f2 0%, var(--clock-accent) 100%);\n            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);\n        }\n        .penalty-banner {\n            background: linear-gradient(100deg, #ff6b57 0%, #e8392a 100%);\n            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);\n        }\n\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <div class=\"scorebug-container\">\n        <!-- Main Scoreboard -->\n        <div class=\"scoreboard\">\n            <!-- Row 1: Hammers -->\n            <div class=\"row\">\n                <div class=\"cell team hammers-team\">\n                    <span class=\"team-name\" data-role=\"teamName\" data-side=\"left\">Hammers</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"cell score hammers-score\">\n                    <span class=\"score-value\" data-role=\"score\" data-side=\"left\">3</span>\n                    <div class=\"banner timeout-banner\" data-role=\"timeoutBanner\" data-side=\"left\" data-live-hidden></div>\n                    <div class=\"banner penalty-banner\" data-role=\"penaltyBanner\" data-side=\"left\" data-live-hidden></div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <!-- Row 2: Pixel Pirates -->\n            <div class=\"row\">\n                <div class=\"cell team pirates-team\">\n                    <span class=\"team-name\" data-role=\"teamName\" data-side=\"right\">Pixel Pirates</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"cell score pirates-score\">\n                    <span class=\"score-value\" data-role=\"score\" data-side=\"right\">1</span>\n                    <div class=\"banner timeout-banner\" data-role=\"timeoutBanner\" data-side=\"right\" data-live-hidden></div>\n                    <div class=\"banner penalty-banner\" data-role=\"penaltyBanner\" data-side=\"right\" data-live-hidden></div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Timer Module -->\n        <div class=\"timer-box\">\n            <div class=\"timer-text\" data-role=\"clock\">4:22</div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n"
        }
      ],
